# Profile: note-writer

A hat that changes something, so it asks first. `card: plan` means that before any tool that
changes something runs, the runtime raises one card: the plan, this profile's `name@version`,
its tools and its success check. Approve lets the run go on. Deny, or no answer, ends it, and
nothing is changed.

The card is raised by the runtime, in code, when the model first calls `write_note`. The model
cannot skip it, and it cannot answer it.

```json
{
  "stew": "2026-11-08-draft",
  "kind": "profile",
  "name": "note-writer",
  "version": 1,
  "for": {
    "task": "add a line to one note"
  },
  "tools": ["read_note", "write_note"],
  "requires": {
    "tool_calling": true,
    "min_context": 4096,
    "structured_output": false,
    "reasoning_effort": false
  },
  "instructions": "Call read_note on the note the request names, then call write_note once with its whole new text.\nKeep every line the note had, and add only what the request asks for.",
  "budgets": {
    "reads": 2,
    "tool_calls": 4,
    "wall_seconds": 180
  },
  "reasoning": "low",
  "gates": {
    "bounds": ["keys"],
    "extra": ["change only the note the request names"]
  },
  "card": "plan",
  "success": {
    "check": "tool_called",
    "args": {
      "tool": "write_note"
    }
  },
  "summary": "<outcome>: <reply>"
}
```
